main='''<main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="/evidence/">Evidence</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Robust leakage witness</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">21 October 2026 Chicago · Gram witness 0.1</div><h1>Allow frequency error.<br>Keep a positive Gram bound.</h1><p class="lede">The finite-mode leakage witness now covers imperfect orthogonality through an exact rational uncertainty bound. A prospective tighter monitor requirement keeps the tail ceiling below 1 mV.</p></div><aside class="callout"><strong>Exact conditional design · Development — no registry entry · Physical promotion 0</strong><p>Frequency, clock, monitor and outside-model bounds remain unmeasured premises. Independent review pending. No experiment, calibration admission or action estimate; EXIT-03 and the circuit candidate stay HOLD.</p></aside><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="/sources/gram-witness-v0.1/THEOREM.md">Read theorem and proof ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gram-witness-v0.1/CERTIFICATE.json">Exact rational certificate</a></div><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>The full uncertainty family is bounded.</h2><p>For 100 nominal integer-Hz modes from 100 through 199, per-mode errors ≤5 mHz and relative one-second monitor-duration error ≤10 ppb give a Gram eigenvalue lower bound above 0.9098. Rational off-diagonal row bounds cover every allowed constant-frequency configuration.</p><p>A common frequency shift cancels from pair differences. Physical band membership, frequency drift and nonlinear time warping still require separate treatment. The monitor-duration bound is distinct from the acquisition’s 0.2 ns timing requirement.</p><table><tbody><tr><th>Measured finite-mode complex RMS</th><td>≤55 µV</td></tr><tr><th>Total waveform monitor L2 error</th><td>≤20 µV</td></tr><tr><th>Outside-model spectral variation</th><td>≤200 µV</td></tr><tr><th>Conditional tail variation</th><td>≤0.99125 mV</td></tr><tr><th>Propagated full-state error / phase</th><td>&lt;0.008667 V / &lt;0.017509 rad</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Small RMS alone is insufficient.</h2><p>Two distinct tones separated by 1 microhertz with opposite 1 V coefficients have spectral variation 2 V but complex RMS below 10 µV on the one-second interval. A separation/coercivity premise prevents that cancellation from concealing large coefficients.</p><p>The old 60 µV RMS share fails the selected robust sufficient budget. The new 55 µV share is a prospective requirement for this witness; the old orthogonal packet remains intact. A directly certified coefficient-error bound is a different route from the waveform-error bound used here.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gram-witness-v0.1/REPORT.md">Controls and practical limits →</a></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>Next connect the witness to sampled measurements.</h2><p>The certificate is exact rational arithmetic. Two floating synthetic eigenvalue diagnostics provide additional checks, not the proof of the uncertainty family. Outside-mode contamination, completeness, normalization and actual monitor accuracy remain independent evidence gates.</p><p>Next bound the sampled-monitor reconstruction using actual sample times, quadrature calibration and numerical error. The candidate estimator cannot serve as its own independent reference.</p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gram-witness-v0.1/certify.py">Certificate replay ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/gram-witness-v0.1/NUMERICAL_DIAGNOSTICS.json">Two synthetic diagnostics →</a><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/calibration-protocol/">Original preparation protocol →</a></div></section></main>'''
